{title: 121 - Go, Tell It On the Mountain}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #121 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 121}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Go, [Bb]tell it on the [F]mountain,
[C]Over the [Dm]hills [C]and [F]ev[Bb]ery[F]where:
[F]Go, [Bb]tell it on the [F]mountain
[Dm]That [Gm]Jesus [F]Christ [C7]is [F]born!
[F]While shepherds kept [Bb]their [F]watching
O’er [C]silent [Dm]flocks [C]by [F]night,
[F]Behold throughout [Bb]the [F]heavens
There [G]shone a [G7]holy [C]li[Dm7]ght.[C7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]Go, tell [Bb]it on [F]the mountain,
[C][Dm]Over [C]the [F]hills [Bb]and [F]everywhere:
[F]Go, tell [Bb]it on [F]the mountain
[Dm]That [Gm]Jesus [F]Christ [C7]is [F]born!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]The [Bb]shepherds feared [F]and trembled
[C][Dm]When [C]lo! [F]Above [Bb]the [F]earth
[F]Rang [Bb]out the [F]angel chorus
[Dm]That [Gm]hailed [F]our [C7]Savior's [F]birth.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Down [Bb]in a [F]lowly manger
[C][Dm]The [C]humble [F]Christ [Bb]was [F]born,
[F]And [Bb]brought us [F]God's salvation
[Dm][Gm]That [F]blessed [C7]Christmas [F]morn.
{end_of_verse}
